{"path":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/policies/index.html","title":"PodGroup Scheduling Policies","description":"Every PodGroup must declare a scheduling policy in its spec.schedulingPolicy field. This policy dictates how the scheduler treats the collection of Pods in the group.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup Scheduling Policies"}]},{"type":"text","value":"FEATURE STATE: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Kubernetes v1.35 [alpha]"},{"type":"text","value":"(disabled by default)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/podgroup-api/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup"}]},{"type":"text","value":" must declare a scheduling policy in its "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"spec.schedulingPolicy"},{"type":"text","value":" field. This policy dictates how the scheduler treats the collection of Pods in the group."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"policy-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Policy types"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/policies/index.html#policy-types","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"schedulingPolicy"},{"type":"text","value":" field supports two policy types: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"basic"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"gang"},{"type":"text","value":". You must specify exactly one."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"basic-policy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic policy"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/policies/index.html#basic-policy","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"basic"},{"type":"text","value":" policy instructs the scheduler to evaluate all Pods on a best-effort basis. Unlike the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"gang"},{"type":"text","value":" policy, a PodGroup using the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"basic"},{"type":"text","value":" policy is considered feasible regardless of how many of its Pods are currently schedulable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The primary reason to use the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"basic"},{"type":"text","value":" policy is to organize Pods into a group for better observability and management, while still evaluating them together within a single, atomic "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/scheduling-eviction/podgroup-scheduling/#podgroup-scheduling-cycle","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup scheduling cycle"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This policy is suited for groups that do not require simultaneous startup but logically belong together, or to open the way for group-level constraints that do not imply \"all-or-nothing\" placement."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"yaml","code":"schedulingPolicy:\n  basic: {}"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"gang-policy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gang policy"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/policies/index.html#gang-policy","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"gang"},{"type":"text","value":" policy enforces \"all-or-nothing\" scheduling. This is essential for tightly-coupled workloads where partial startup results in deadlocks or wasted resources."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This can be used for "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/job/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Jobs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or any other batch process where all workers must run concurrently to make progress."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"gang"},{"type":"text","value":" policy requires a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"minCount"},{"type":"text","value":" field, which is the minimum number of Pods that must be schedulable simultaneously for the group to be feasible:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"yaml","code":"schedulingPolicy:\n  gang:\n    # The number of Pods that must be schedulable simultaneously\n    # for the group to be admitted.\n    minCount: 4"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"setting-policies-via-podgrouptemplates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting policies via PodGroupTemplates"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/policies/index.html#setting-policies-via-podgrouptemplates","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using the "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workload API"}]},{"type":"text","value":", you define scheduling policies inside "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroupTemplates"},{"type":"text","value":". The workload controller copies the policy from the template into each PodGroup it creates, making the PodGroup self-contained. Changes to the Workload's templates only affect newly created PodGroups, not existing ones."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For standalone PodGroups (created without a Workload), you set "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"spec.schedulingPolicy"},{"type":"text","value":" directly on the PodGroup itself."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"what-s-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What's next"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/policies/index.html#what-s-next","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/podgroup-api/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup API"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for how policies are carried at runtime."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Learn about the "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workload API"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that defines PodGroupTemplates."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read about "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/scheduling-eviction/podgroup-scheduling/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup scheduling"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read about the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/scheduling-eviction/gang-scheduling/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"gang scheduling"}]},{"type":"text","value":" algorithm."}]}]}]}}
